  "details": "With more additions to the Quick Menu and Action Menu, as well as the release of Main Menu 2.0, both seasoned and newer users should be entitled to knowing the full functionality of the menus.\nPreviously, in early 2018, VRChat had a world featured called \"Help Videos\". It summarized VRChat concepts, and parts of the menu into short videos to give an overview of how to navigate through the application.\nWhile it's difficult to inform users of every update in video form, it would be more simple to write it in blog form. That's the route VRChat has taken, which is understandable. Problem is: not everyone wants to read it, or has the attention span to. The Help Videos world is over four years old, and does not reflect what VRChat is now. (VRChat has come such a long way! :])\nFor those who do want to read about VRChat updates: The Articles tab is on Main Menu 2.0, but the Quick Menu banners are outdated, need a cleanup, and the blog post about the Quick Menu update returns as a 404 error.\n(See also: https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/please-clean-up-launch-pad-banners)\nThe Tutorial World is hardly a tutorial, as it only makes you choose a public avatar, shows a graphic on how to move (not exactly necessary), and drops you into a public world. That's all there is to it; it's not considered a tutorial. It fails to inform new users on how to perform basic actions.\nAs an opportunity to expand the VRChat Learning Channel, which has not been touched in over nine months and has a minimal amount of content: creating bite-sized videos to skim all the VRChat menus and actions would be beneficial to the userbase if it was made viewable in a Tutorial world, shared in a blog, or posted anywhere on VRChat's media channels.",
